From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:08:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: bind only the entry of a Wi-Fi local-in session

A session of the Wi-Fi local fastpath records the PPE entry of its
flow one time, from the hash of a received packet. It recorded a
software hash or an index outside of the table too, and the fastpath
bound the entry of each later packet without a compare. A bound
entry that no session holds has no path to the stack, so the
fastpath drops its frames.

A session now records only a valid hardware index, and the fastpath
binds only the entry that the session holds. A flow with another
index, or with index 0, stays on the normal receive path.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c |   12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
@@ -914,12 +914,22 @@ static unsigned int wifi_lo_nf_hook_loca
 		return NF_ACCEPT;
 	}
 
+	if (!skb->l4_hash || skb->sw_hash)
+		goto out;
+
 	hash = FOE_ENTRY_NUM(skb);
-	if (hash != 0 && READ_ONCE(lo->hash) == 0)
+	if (!hash || !glb_eth || hash >= glb_eth->soc->ppe_sram_etry_num)
+		goto out;
+
+	if (READ_ONCE(lo->hash) == 0)
 		wifi_lo_hash_publish(lo, hash);
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(lo->hash) != hash)
+		goto out;
+
 	pinfo.magic = PPE_MAGIC_LOCAL_IN_NS;
 	airoha_ppe_tx_handler(skb, &pinfo, 0);
+out:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 	return NF_ACCEPT;
